    "digdeeper": {
      "type": "zeta-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Description",
            "content": "<p>D+K 5000 is a complex of vitamin K2 and vitamin D3. It delivers vitamin K2 as <strong>menaquinone-7 (MK-7)</strong> — the most bioavailable and bioactive form of K2 — alongside <strong>vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol)</strong>, the identical form your body synthesizes when sunlight hits your skin.</p><p>Historical use and decades of clinical research support the role of vitamin K supplementation in bone and cardiovascular health. Vitamin D3 supports immune function, mood, hormone balance, and bone health. Together, they make the daily-foundation duo most adults are quietly short on.</p><p><strong>Clinical Applications</strong></p><ul><li>Supports bone health by promoting carboxylation of bone proteins</li><li>Supports cardiovascular health by influencing arterial calcium deposits</li><li>Supports healthy blood clotting</li><li>Supports immune function</li><li>Supports calcium absorption and utilization</li></ul><p><em>*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</em></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ingredients",
            "content": "<p><strong>Supplement Facts</strong></p><p><strong>Serving size:</strong> 1 vegetarian capsule · <strong>Servings per bottle:</strong> 60</p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin D3 (as cholecalciferol)</strong> — 125 mcg · 5000 IU</li><li><strong>Vitamin K2 (as menaquinone-7, MK-7)</strong> — 90 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Other Ingredients</strong></p><p>Hypromellose (vegetarian capsule), microcrystalline cellulose, medium-chain triglycerides, silica.</p><p><strong>Why these forms</strong></p><p>MK-7 has a half-life of about three days in the body — much longer than other K2 forms (MK-4 lasts about an hour). That means one daily capsule maintains steady levels.</p><p>D3 (cholecalciferol) is the same molecule your skin makes from sunlight — far more bioavailable than D2.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Directions & Precautions",
            "content": "<p><strong>Take 1 capsule daily, with a meal that has some fat</strong> — eggs, avocado, olive oil, yogurt, whatever you eat. D3 and K2 are fat-soluble; they absorb best with food.</p><p><strong>Best Time</strong></p><p>Morning or midday works best for most people. D3 can be mildly energizing — so we don't recommend it right before sleep.</p><p><strong>Pairs Well With</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ZETA MULTI</strong> — the daily Foundation of vitamins and minerals (covers everything D+K doesn't)</li><li><strong>ZETA MEGAS</strong> — omega-3s for the same fat-soluble absorption pathway</li><li><strong>ZETA LONGEVITY</strong> — for the long game</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><p>If you're on blood thinners (warfarin, Coumadin), check with your physician before starting D+K — vitamin K can interact with these medications. If pregnant, nursing, or under 18, consult your healthcare provider. Don't exceed the recommended serving.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Research",
            "content": "<p>A few of the studies we lean on. We won't pretend it's a complete bibliography — but it's the work that shaped the formula.</p><p><strong>Schwalfenberg GK.</strong> Vitamins K1 and K2: The Emerging Group of Vitamins Required for Human Health. <em>Journal of Nutrition and Metabolism</em>, 2017.</p><p><strong>Beulens JWJ et al.</strong> The role of menaquinones (vitamin K2) in human health. <em>British Journal of Nutrition</em>, 2013.</p><p><strong>Holick MF.</strong> Vitamin D deficiency. <em>New England Journal of Medicine</em>, 2007.</p><p><strong>Knapen MHJ et al.</strong> Three-year low-dose menaquinone-7 supplementation helps decrease bone loss in healthy postmenopausal women. <em>Osteoporosis International</em>, 2013.</p><p><strong>Geleijnse JM et al.</strong> Dietary intake of menaquinone is associated with a reduced risk of coronary heart disease: the Rotterdam Study. <em>Journal of Nutrition</em>, 2004.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
      },
